0 Fixture: cones that leave the plug room and then stand in the wire.
0 Expected: problems -- the cable zone of both ports is fouled.
0
0 This is the subtler half of the port problem. At x = +-50 a cone misses
0 the plug's 34-wide shell (x = 23..57 only for the first 20 LDU, and the
0 cone starts at z = 70, one LDU past it). It then sits squarely in the
0 ribbon that leaves the plug along the same axis, x = 31..49. You can
0 seat the plug; the wire then leans on a 1x1 cone held by one stud.
0
0 The cones two studs further out, at x = +-70, are the version that
0 works -- see good-hub-ports-clear.ldr.
0
